From: j7prime p2 <p2@j7prime.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:56:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] arm64: dts: exynos7870-on7xelte: enable CPU DVFS,
 thermal and idle

Wire up what the SoC patches before this one provide:

- cpu-supply = BUCK1 (VDD_CPU, shared by both clusters) and one
  operating-points-v2 table per cluster for cpufreq-dt. The tables list
  the ECT levels with a voltage in the vendor ASV table, at ASV table 5
  group 5 + 25 mV (Fontana's SM-T580 values), which is at or above
  Burak's measured SM-J701F vendor voltages + 12.5 mV at every level.
  The ceiling is 1248 MHz for the bring-up; 1352/1482/1586 MHz (vendor
  maximum) are present with status "disabled". The OPP voltage ranges
  reach up to the regulator maximum so the requests of the two clusters
  aggregate on the shared rail.
- A fixed 100 us settling time after every BUCK1 rise: the s2mps11
  driver does not program the BUCK1 ramp rate on the S2MPU05, so the
  12 mV/us of the DT is not guaranteed by the hardware.
- The SoC thermal zone on the TMU, with the TMU node enabled: passive
  trips at 80 C (both clusters to 902.2 MHz) and 90 C (546 MHz), hot at
  100 C, critical at 110 C (vendor hardware trip: 115 C).
- The PSCI core power-down idle state (vendor CPU_SLEEP parameter
  0x10000), registered switched off by cpuidle-psci on this SoC.

Origin: j7prime p2 series. OPP tables and cpu-supply wiring follow
Alessandro Fontana's exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts (gtaxlwifi/7.3,
d1979ff14a1d); idle state after Burak's exynos7870-j7velte-cpuidle.dts;
trips chosen for this phone.
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---

Notes:
    Origin: new in the j7prime p2 series for v7.3.4 (see the Origin line in the message).

